        "original_id": "dcb5ad79-e835-586d-b776-98b0dd82d94a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Connell, Robert Connell, Berthold Viertel, Paul Muni\n- Works: Seven Faces, A Friend of Napoleon, The Most Dangerous Game, The Hounds of Zaroff, Bloodlust!\n- Publications: The Saturday Evening Post, Collier's\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" was published in The Saturday Evening Post on June 30, 1923.\n- Richard Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff,\" was first published in Collier's on January 19, 1924.\n- The film Seven Faces was based on Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- Seven Faces was directed by Berthold Viertel and starred Paul Muni in his second screen appearance.\n- Richard Connell's best known work was \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" which was filmed three years later.\n- Bloodlust! is a 1961 American horror thriller film based on Robert Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
